# Module-wide options. Every symbol carries the BEACON_ prefix so the module
# can share a manifest with prospector-zmk-module (PROSPECTOR_*, ZMK_STATUS_ADV_*)
# while canon migrates from it.

menu "Beacon"

config BEACON_BACKLIGHT_BRIGHTNESS
    int "Backlight brightness at boot (percent)"
    range 0 100
    default 80
    depends on LED_PWM
    help
      Duty cycle written to the pwm-leds backlight before the display driver
      starts. The unit has no ambient light sensor, so this value is fixed for
      the whole runtime.

config BEACON_BOOTLOADER_ON_1200_BAUD
    bool "Enter the UF2 bootloader on a 1200 baud touch"
    depends on USB_CDC_ACM && RETENTION_BOOT_MODE
    select CDC_ACM_DTE_RATE_CALLBACK_SUPPORT
    help
      When the host sets any CDC ACM port of the device to 1200 baud (for
      example "stty -f /dev/cu.usbmodemXXXX 1200" on macOS), set the retained
      boot mode to bootloader and warm-reboot 250 ms later, so the UF2
      bootloader mounts its drive without a reset double-tap. The delay lets
      the host's control transfer complete before the device resets.

      Any program that sets the port to 1200 baud, a serial monitor included,
      reboots the device. The prospector shield turns this on by default
      because the unit has no key for &bootloader and no touch input.

config BEACON_SPRITE_GIF
    string "GIF sprite embedded in the image (absolute path, empty = none)"
    default ""
    depends on SHIELD_PROSPECTOR && ZMK_DISPLAY_STATUS_SCREEN_CUSTOM
    help
      Absolute path of a GIF89a file with a global colour table (the only
      kind LVGL's gifdec opens). The build embeds its bytes in the image and
      the status screen plays it above the battery readings, scaled by the
      largest whole factor that fits (or filling the space above them, see
      BEACON_SPRITE_FILL), at three quarters of the GIF's own tempo while
      nobody types; while the keyboard is typed on it runs on the key presses
      instead (eight frames queued per press, stepped one per render and
      skipped as presses pile up), and 0.2 s after the last press arrived the
      frames still queued are dropped and the tempo resumes (src/sprite.c,
      src/prospector_screen.c). Empty: no sprite, which is what CI and the
      release build.

      The decoder keeps 5 bytes per pixel plus 16 KiB in the LVGL pool for
      the whole run; the build fails when that does not fit
      CONFIG_LV_Z_MEM_POOL_SIZE (the prospector shield's default grows with a
      sprite, boards/shields/prospector/Kconfig.defconfig). Local builds:
      scripts/build.sh --sprite <gif> [--sprite-name <text>].

config BEACON_SPRITE
    bool
    default y if BEACON_SPRITE_GIF != ""
    select LV_USE_IMAGE
    select LV_USE_GIF
    select LV_GIF_CACHE_DECODE_DATA
    imply SYS_HEAP_RUNTIME_STATS if LOG
    help
      Set when BEACON_SPRITE_GIF names a file. LV_GIF_CACHE_DECODE_DATA is a
      correctness requirement here, not a speed option (src/sprite.c). With
      logging on, the sprite's minute line reports the LVGL pool's allocated
      and peak bytes, the numbers the pool size is chosen from.

config BEACON_SPRITE_FILL
    bool "Let the sprite fill the space above the battery readings"
    depends on SHIELD_PROSPECTOR && ZMK_DISPLAY_STATUS_SCREEN_CUSTOM
    help
      With a sprite (BEACON_SPRITE_GIF) it is scaled by the largest factor of
      its proportions that fits between the top edge and the readings, whole
      or not (a GIF pixel then covers 2 or 3 panel pixels in turn; a 90x90 px
      GIF shows at about 2.2x above the HP bar on 280x240, 2x when the bar
      carries a sprite name), 2 px in from the edges, standing on the
      readings, which keep their 12 px margin (the panel's corners are
      rounded). Without a sprite the readings show as usual, so a consumer
      can keep the option in its conf while CI and the release build without
      a GIF.

config BEACON_SPRITE_NAME
    string "Name of the sprite, shown under the HP bar (empty = none)"
    default ""
    depends on BEACON_SPRITE
    help
      With the HP bar (BEACON_READINGS_HP_BAR) the text is a second row of
      its box, at the left in unscii 16, and the box grows from 28 to 46 px,
      so the sprite's space loses 18 rows (a 90x90 px GIF filling it shows at
      2x, 180x180, instead of about 2.2x). 15 glyphs fit; a longer name is
      cut. Printable ASCII only: the font has no other glyphs, a double quote
      or a backslash would need Kconfig escaping, and "??" would be a C
      trigraph in autoconf.h. The digits show no name. Empty: no second row
      and a 28 px box, the screen of CI and the release build, which have no
      sprite.

      Like the GIF, the name is a personal file's and never goes into a
      repository: a local build passes it (scripts/build.sh --sprite <gif>
      --sprite-name <text>, through a Kconfig fragment so that a failed
      configure step, whose command line west prints, shows only the
      fragment's path; canon derives it from the GIF's file name with its
      assets/sprite-name.sh).

choice BEACON_READINGS
    prompt "Battery readings"
    default BEACON_READINGS_DIGITS
    depends on SHIELD_PROSPECTOR && ZMK_DISPLAY_STATUS_SCREEN_CUSTOM

config BEACON_READINGS_DIGITS
    bool "Digits in the bottom corners"
    help
      Each half's battery as a percentage in Montserrat 48, the left half
      bottom-left, the right half bottom-right; "--" without a reading, grey
      without a payload in the last minute.

config BEACON_READINGS_HP_BAR
    bool "One HP bar at the bottom"
    select LV_USE_BAR
    select LV_FONT_UNSCII_16
    help
      A battle-screen HP bar, "HP" and a bar with its value on it ("65/100")
      in one dark box along the bottom. Its length is the keyboard's
      battery: the mean of the halves with a reading, or the one half that
      has one. Green from 50 %, yellow from 20 %, red below; an empty track
      and "--/100" without a reading, all grey without a payload in the last
      minute. With BEACON_SPRITE_NAME the name is a second row of the box.
      Text in unscii 16, a 16 px pixel font.

config BEACON_READINGS_NONE
    bool "None while a sprite shows"
    help
      No readings while a sprite shows, and the sprite may use the whole
      panel. Without a sprite (CI, the release build), or when the sprite
      stops on malformed GIF data, the digits show, so the conf stays valid
      for those builds.

endchoice

config BEACON_STATUS_BROADCAST
    bool "Broadcast the keyboard's status on a second advertising set"
    depends on ZMK_SPLIT_ROLE_CENTRAL && BT && SETTINGS
    select BT_EXT_ADV
    help
      On the keyboard's split central, advertise the status payload (each
      half's battery, the highest active layer and its name, and a count of
      key presses; src/status_payload.h) as manufacturer data in a legacy,
      non-connectable, non-scannable advertising set next to ZMK's own
      connectable one. The Prospector Dongle's observer (the prospector
      shield) reads it.

      The consumer's config must also set CONFIG_BT_EXT_ADV_MAX_ADV_SET=2:
      with BT_EXT_ADV the host takes ZMK's legacy advertising from the same
      pool of sets, and the build fails on a pool of 1. BT_EXT_ADV costs
      about 34 KB of flash and 11 KB of RAM on nRF52840 and switches the host
      to the extended HCI commands (canon imprint_dongle, 2026-09-26).

config BEACON_STATUS_BROADCAST_INTERVAL_MS
    int "Advertising interval of the status set (ms)"
    depends on BEACON_STATUS_BROADCAST
    range 20 10240
    default 200
    help
      The payload is refreshed once per interval and right after a key
      press, so a scanner sees a new battery or layer value after at most two
      intervals and a new key count after at most one (plus the advertiser's
      random delay of up to 10 ms). The sprite's KEY_GRACE_MS and the
      observer's KEYS_DELTA_MAX (src/sprite.c, src/status_observer.c) are
      tuned to the default of 200 ms; revisit them with a different value.

endmenu
